{
  "borough": "Wandsworth",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The applicant has failed to demonstrate that the existing HMO (sui generis) cannot meet appropriate standards and has no realistic prospect of doing. The submitted structural and market evidence does not demonstrate that refurbishment to HMO standard would be unachievable or unviable, and no justification has been provided as to why works proposed for a single dwelling could not equally enable continued HMO use. In the absence of adequate replacement HMO provision, the proposal would result in the unjustified loss of an HMO and harm to local housing provision within the borough. For the given reasons the proposal is contrary to Policy LP29B of the Wandsworth Local Plan and Policy H9 of the London Plan.",
    "Reason : 2 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to make available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the principle of the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
